{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>caught in a thicket.</b> Pesikta: He said to Abraham: See your children who will come after you — when they are entangled and caught in transgressions, what will they do? They will sound the horns before Me and I will recall for them the binding of Isaac and acquit them in judgment. And what is the nature of the shofar? It takes in through this and lets out through this — so too your children: even if they have many accusers, I will take them in through this and will not listen to them. Therefore Moses said to Israel: The shofar is your advocate — sound the shofar on Rosh HaShanah, so that the Holy One, blessed be He, will recall for you the binding of Isaac, and you will be acquitted in judgment."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:48.663212782Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}